  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-PAK801</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The strategy is to support Employers Federation of Pakistan to engage at the macro level with state institutions for policy making but also joint development frameworks of the UN, including the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework. The launch of the Pakistan Business Taskforce (PBTF) roadmap for the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) envisioned during the biennium will mark a significant step in improving business involvement in achieving the SDGs. The roadmap focuses on collating information about the contributions of businesses to the SDGs, strengthening the Employers Federation of Pakistan&apos;s (EFP) institutional capacity, and enhancing its ability to provide business leadership. Through PBTF, EFP aims to present a unified and coordinated representation of the private sector while effectively engaging in policy dialogue and participating in the UNSDCF process.

EFP is actively working with the UN Resident Coordinator (UNRC) and various UN agencies to strengthen its engagement with the PBTF. As part of this effort, a strategy is being developed for an advocacy campaign aimed at promoting the SDGs. This campaign will be followed by a report to track its progress and impact.

In addition to supporting the EFP, the strategy also focuses on building the capacity of social partners to enhance the institutional structure, allowing for better responses to employers&#x2019; needs. These efforts are crucial for ensuring that the private sector plays an active and effective role in advancing the SDGs in Pakistan.</narrative>
  </description>
